.TH ACER\-POWERSAVE\-SESSION 1 "September 2026" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
acer\-powersave\-session \- panel refresh rate following the power profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acer\-powersave\-session
.SH DESCRIPTION
Changes the panel refresh rate according to the active profile of
.BR power\-profiles\-daemon (8).
.PP
It runs as a user service rather than inside the system daemon because
.BR kscreen\-doctor (1)
needs the user's Wayland session, which root does not have.
.PP
Plasma does not offer this: PowerDevil states explicitly that it does not
manage display configuration.
.PP
Measured on a Predator PH315\-53, dropping the panel from 144 to 60 Hz saves
about 400 mW, the single largest saving found on that machine.
.SH USAGE
.nf
.RS
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now acer\-powersave\-session.service
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/acer-powersave-session.conf
Overrides PANEL and RES, and the HZ_POWER_SAVER, HZ_BALANCED and
HZ_PERFORMANCE values.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acer\-powersave (1),
.BR kscreen\-doctor (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Antonio Orizondo Leyva
